      "updated": 1785520578691,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "-- Sleep-polling trades CPU waste for latency. \nIf a task arrives 1ms after a worker goes to sleep with a 100ms sleep interval, \nthat task waits nearly 100ms before being processed. \nYou're stuck choosing between high latency (long sleep) or high CPU usage (short sleep).\n\n*** Example of process requests asynchronously:\n-- Email sending: email sending success, worker grab email to process (enqueue)\n-- Image upload service:  The upload API saves the original to a temp location, \nenqueues a processing task, and returns success immediately. \nWorkers pull tasks, resize images, upload to S3, and update the database with the new URLs.\n-- Payment process:  Save the order, enqueue a fulfillment task, respond to the user. \nWorkers handle the multi-step process. One failure doesn't block the whole flow.\n-- Report generation: Save a \"pending\" report record, enqueue a generation task, \nand return \"Your report is being generated.\" \nWorkers pull tasks, run the query, generate the CSV, \nupload to S3, and mark the report complete. The admin polls or gets notified when ready.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "-- Sleep-polling trades CPU waste for latency. \nIf a task arrives 1ms after a worker goes to sleep with a 100ms sleep interval, \nthat task waits nearly 100ms before being processed. \nYou're stuck choosing between high latency (long sleep) or high CPU usage (short sleep).\n\n*** Example of process requests asynchronously:\n-- Email sending: email sending success, worker grab email to process (enqueue)\n-- Image upload service:  The upload API saves the original to a temp location, \nenqueues a processing task, and returns success immediately. \nWorkers pull tasks, resize images, upload to S3, and update the database with the new URLs.\n-- Payment process:  Save the order, enqueue a fulfillment task, respond to the user. \nWorkers handle the multi-step process. One failure doesn't block the whole flow.\n-- Report generation: Save a \"pending\" report record, enqueue a generation task, \nand return \"Your report is being generated.\" \nWorkers pull tasks, run the query, generate the CSV, \nupload to S3, and mark the report complete. The admin polls or gets notified when ready.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "IysQhaSz3Dfiv2ADeBDQi",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 85.34284261142545,
      "y": 2098.468547185715,
      "width": 1088.8193359375,
      "height": 225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1i",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 930833395,
      "version": 527,
      "versionNonce": 1836916509,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785520580615,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "*** Example of handle bursty traffic (with controlled rate)\n-- New sites with 1000 page view/minute --> 100000 page view/minute ==> \nThe web servers enqueue page view events. Analytics workers process them at a steady rate. \nThe queue absorbs the spike. Without it, your analytics database gets crushed and the whole site slows down.\n-- Batch job completion: enqueue 10mil job and worker send notifications at controlled rate\n-- Webhooks: Webhook handle enqueue events, queue prevent burst from causing DB connection exhaustion\n\n\n ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "*** Example of handle bursty traffic (with controlled rate)\n-- New sites with 1000 page view/minute --> 100000 page view/minute ==> \nThe web servers enqueue page view events. Analytics workers process them at a steady rate. \nThe queue absorbs the spike. Without it, your analytics database gets crushed and the whole site slows down.\n-- Batch job completion: enqueue 10mil job and worker send notifications at controlled rate\n-- Webhooks: Webhook handle enqueue events, queue prevent burst from causing DB connection exhaustion\n\n\n ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
